 "input_sha256": "86aaf7ca41be60140f11dd4fed84bffed2590746dcb267d4e9947128974336be",
 "explanation": "Dependencies: n°15 through its 1.6.6.0 copy patch/os_send_merge_1660.json (this patch takes two of its words: the Voice refresh call [address] and the F_VOICE byte call [address]), n°1, n°24 and n°39 (request chain: the command reaches [address] in v0), n°27 (standard packer), n°58 (pad channel table [address]). Why: a full backup of the machine before any Voice OS install. The Debug menu only dumps voice 0, and a Voice chip's dump pointer is 16 bits (TBLPAG forced to 0) and never reset, so its stream repeats every 98,304 bytes and only the 1st, 4th, 7th... dump after power-on starts at PC 0. A. Alignment: the two sites that read a Voice byte ([routine] [address] and OS_DUMP's last two bytes of a block [address]) call VDUMP_BYTE, which counts the byte in POS[chip] (mod 98,304) and reads it from chip CHIP (0 unless a backup runs; bounded to 0-5 before the select table, whose entries 6 and 7 are not chip selects); before a dump, ALIGN reads and drops (98,304 - POS) mod 98,304 bytes, so every dump starts at PC 0 with the boot page and the calibration. The Debug menu's Voice dump aligns before its header and keeps SysEx 72 and voice 0. B. Request F0 01 28 44 F7, on the cable set in System (the only cable the SysEx parser accepts), answered on that cable, drawing nothing: F0 01 28 78+k <voice k, 64 blocks> F7 for k = 0-5, F0 01 28 75 <Main boot flash 0xBFC00000-0xBFC02FFF, configuration words included, 12 blocks> F7, then F0 01 28 76 <235 bytes in the standard 7-bit packing: 7 (System file version), the 202 settings [address], the 32 pad channels of n°58> F7. 78-7D and 75 have the OS-dump layout (1,024-byte blocks packed one by one, 14-bit checksum, tools/dsi_unpack.py decodes them); none of these ids is an update command, so a backup sent back starts nothing. Hook: [routine] [address] calls BACKUP_CHECK with the command in v0 (moved instruction in the delay slot, the replaced sltiu given back on return); for 0x44 the backup runs, then 0x44 goes on through n°1 and n°24 to [routine](0), as 0x43 does. Reads only: SPI words 0xF800 / 0xFF00, loads through KSEG1, RAM loads; no flash write. RAM: [address] CHIP, [address] POS[6] (.bss hole, zero at boot). Main loop only; 203 words at 0x9d07ac80-0x9d07afab and 5 hook words. Proof: tools/sim_full_backup.py and its counter-proofs; Docs/analyses/feature-full-backup.md.",
